=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">s</span> <span class=\"fn\">x</span></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#And\">∧</a> <span class=\"fn\">y</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">f</span> <span class=\"fn\">x</span></span></span></span>)</span> →\n    <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Internal/Order/Basic.html#Lean.Order.PreservesSup\">Lean.Order.PreservesSup</a> <span class=\"fn\">f</span></span></span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Std/Internal/Order/Basic.html#Lean.Order.PreservesSup.mk","kind":"ctor","line":140,"name":"Lean.Order.PreservesSup.mk","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/Internal/Order/Basic.lean#L140-L153"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">class</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Internal/Order/Basic.html#Lean.Order.PreservesSup\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Order</span>.<span class=\"name\">PreservesSup</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">[<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Internal/Order/Basic.html#Lean.Order.CompleteLattice\">CompleteLattice</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span>]</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">f</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">α</span> → <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Prop</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`f : α → α` *preserves suprema* if it distributes over arbitrary suprema:\n`f (sup s) = sup { f x | x ∈ s }`. Equivalently `f` is a lower adjoint, so it has an upper adjoint\n`PreservesSup.upperAdjoint f`.\n\nA frame operator acts by a supremum-preserving map for each resource `r`: the lattice meet\n`(a ⊓ ·)`,\nor a cost combinator `(costConj r)` for a counter resource. The upper adjoint is the corresponding\nimplication: Heyting `⇨` for the meet, a magic wand for separating conjunction.","docLink":"./Std/Internal/Order/Basic.html#Lean.Order.PreservesSup","kind":"class","line":140,"name":"Lean.Order.PreservesSup","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/Internal/Order/Basic.lean#L140-L153"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Internal/Order/Basic.html#Lean.Order.«term⌜_⌝»\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Order</span>.<span class=\"name\">«term⌜_⌝»</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.ParserDescr\">ParserDescr</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Embedding of propositions into an CompleteLattice type. `⌜p⌝` embeds `p : Prop` as `⊤` if `p` holds\nand `⊥` otherwise.","docLink":"./Std/Internal/Order/Basic.html#Lean.Order.«term⌜_⌝»","kind":"def","line":125,"name":"Lean.Order.«term⌜_⌝»","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/Internal/Order/Basic.lean#L125-L126"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">noncomputable def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Internal/Order/Basic.html#Lean.Order.CompleteLattice.ofProp\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Order</span>.<span class=\"name\">CompleteLattice</span>.<span class=\"name\">ofProp</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">l</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u_1}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><